Hi.
i am trying to build GREP application on hadoop using rhipe. For this
i have a text file where each line consist of words. This file resided
on Hadoop distributed file system.

For this i have created a mapper function whose responsibility is to
1. Sequence along the characters from "a" to "z",which are my keys.
2. For each character grep all the words in which the character is
appearing. For this i am using R grep() function. These vector of
words would be my "values" to the keys.

For example:
 for key "a" the values could be "and", "bad", "amazon" etc
for key "b" the values could be "bad", "boss" etc.. (Note there would
be duplication of words)

i am using rhlapply function for running the map-reduce job. But
1. i dont know how to write the function which will read the input
file from the  HDFS.

2. MoreOver it throws error saying that "in.txt" is not a sequential
file, i tried giving the directory but it gives me the same error.
After studying i found RHIPE expects the data to be in key value
pairs. so i need to perform the same operation as the mapper function
before only.

createRhipeList<-function(x)
{
        for(i in 1:26)
        d1<-list(k=letters[i],v=grep(letters[i],myData,value=TRUE))

}

